  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1204 AM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\n\nPredominantly dry. Temps overall will be in the 60s plains and \n50s valley. Monday should be the warmest day of the week with \nsome L70s over the plains and upper 50s in the valleys. Coolest \nday is expected to be Wed as a modest, albeit dry, mid level \nshort wave drops southeast over the region. Max temps over the \nplains are expected to fall into the 60-65F range while mid 50s \nare expected over the valleys. We will likely see breezy \nconditions on this day.\n\nIf we see any precip during this period, it will likely be Sunday as \na leading short wave in advance of a large Pacific trough moves into \nthe region. However, models do not unanimously agree with this \nas the Euro is slower while the GFS is quicker with the system. \nDESI statistical guidance keeps it dry over the region.\n\nBased on the longer range guidance, the better chance of seeing \nprecip returning to the region will be late next week. \n\\/Hodanish",
